<?xml version="1.0" ?>
<usx version="3.0">
  <book code="2JN" style="id">2 JOHN</book>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" sid="2JN 1"/>
  <para style="s1">Greeting</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="2JN 1:1"/>
    The Elder,
    <verse eid="2JN 1:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">To the elect lady and her children, whom I genuinely love in the truth—and not I alone, but all who have come to know the truth—</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="2JN 1:2"/>
    because of the truth that abides within us and will remain with us forever:
    <verse eid="2JN 1:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="2JN 1:3"/>
    Grace, mercy, and peace will be with us from God the Father and from Jesus Christ, the Son of the Father, in truth and love.
    <verse eid="2JN 1:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Walking According to God’s Commandments</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="2JN 1:4"/>
    It brought me great joy to discover that some of your children are living according to the truth, just as we received commandment from the Father.
    <verse eid="2JN 1:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="2JN 1:5"/>
    And now I appeal to you, dear lady—not as though I were writing a new commandment, but one we have had from the beginning—that we love one another.
    <verse eid="2JN 1:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="2JN 1:6"/>
    And this is what love means: that we live in obedience to His commandments. This is the commandment you have heard from the beginning, that you must live in love.
    <verse eid="2JN 1:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">The Emergence of the Deceivers</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="2JN 1:7"/>
    For many deceivers have gone out into the world, those who do not confess Jesus Christ as having come in the flesh. Such a person is the deceiver and the antichrist.
    <verse eid="2JN 1:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="2JN 1:8"/>
    Guard yourselves, so that you do not forfeit what we have labored for, but may receive a full reward.
    <verse eid="2JN 1:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="2JN 1:9"/>
    Anyone who goes beyond the teaching of Christ and does not remain in it does not possess God. The one who remains in the teaching possesses both the Father and the Son.
    <verse eid="2JN 1:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="2JN 1:10"/>
    If anyone comes to you and does not bring this teaching, do not receive him into your home or offer him a greeting,
    <verse eid="2JN 1:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="2JN 1:11"/>
    for the one who greets him participates in his evil deeds.
    <verse eid="2JN 1:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Farewell Greeting</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="2JN 1:12"/>
    Though I have many things to write to you, I do not wish to do so with paper and ink. Instead, I hope to come to you and speak face to face, so that our joy may be made complete.
    <verse eid="2JN 1:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="2JN 1:13"/>
    The children of your elect sister send you their greetings.
    <verse eid="2JN 1:13"/>
  </para>
  <chapter eid="2JN 1"/>
</usx>
